Approved fix:
Product Owner repair for Story `halve-negative` (file: `docs/product/product.yaml` owns the concepts; the Story document owns the Item). Only acceptance criterion `001-even` blocks the Story. Apply at the menu only; no architecture binding is required.

## Why

The `then` step of `001-even` reads `the result is satisfying`. The `then` concept `result` means: "The halve command succeeds and prints exactly a stated integer, the half rounded toward zero." "satisfying" names no integer, so no objective stdout assertion can be written without inventing the value. "satisfying" is also an evaluative qualifier of the same family as the forbidden `properly` / `correctly` / `appropriate`.

The expected value is already fixed by the product document description: "Negative inputs -6, -7 and -1 produce -3, -3 and 0 respectively." Stating `-3` therefore records existing intent and adds no scope.

## Exact change

In the `acceptance_criteria` list of Story `halve-negative`, replace this block:

```yaml
    - id: 001-even
      description: The calculator must return a satisfying result when the Calculator User halves -6.
      steps:
        - given:
            - the number is "-6"
        - when:
            - the Calculator User halves the number
        - then:
            - the result is satisfying
```

with this block:

```yaml
    - id: 001-even
      description: The calculator must return -3 when the Calculator User halves -6.
      steps:
        - given:
            - the number is "-6"
        - when:
            - the Calculator User halves the number
        - then:
            - the result is "-3"
```

Two edits only:
1. `description`: "a satisfying result" becomes "-3", matching the phrasing already used by `002-odd` and `003-near-zero`.
2. The single `then` step: `the result is satisfying` becomes `the result is "-3"`.

## What stays unchanged

- The `id` `001-even`, and both the `given` and `when` steps, verbatim.
- Acceptance criteria `002-odd` and `003-near-zero` in full — both already convert.
- Every other Story field: `feature: calculator`, `title`, `as_a`, `i_want`, `so_that`, `status: PLANNED`.
- All concepts in `docs/product/product.yaml`. No new concept and no new variation: `the result is "-3"` is the same item and use as the existing `then` concept `result`, in the identical form already used by `002-odd` and `003-near-zero`, so the existing concept covers it as written.
- `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml`. The service `calculator` already declares `public_interface.kind: cli`, which is the only interface kind the sketches use. No binding, helper, or architecture edit is needed.

## Effect

With that one edit, `001-even` becomes a runnable CLI sketch:

GIVEN number -6 / WHEN run `calculator halve -6` once / THEN exit code 0 AND stdout == "-3" exactly (half rounded toward zero)

Convertibility goes from 2/3 = 66.7% to 3/3 = 100%, above the 80% threshold.

